# Agent Git Workflow

When doing feature work that will be committed:

## 1. Start (run first)

- `git checkout main && git pull origin main`
- `git checkout -b feature/<branch-name>` (use a short, descriptive name, e.g. `feature/quality-gates`)

## 2. Work

- Make changes. Reference files with `@path` when relevant.
- Do not run `git add .`. Stage only the files you changed.

## 3. Finish (run last)

- `git add <file1> <file2> ...` (specific paths only)
- `git commit -m "type: short description"` (e.g. `docs: add agent workflow`)
- `git push origin feature/<branch-name>`
- Remind: open a PR; do not merge to main directly. CI must be green before merging.

If the user provides a branch name (e.g. in a header like `BRANCH: feature/xyz`), use that for the feature branch.
